{
  "analysis": "The VM decoder supports a MIPS32 subset including SPECIAL2 MUL/CLZ and SPECIAL3 EXT/BSHFL. The remaining challenge is that glibc would use standard Linux syscall numbers, which do not match the VM's syscall numbers, so a normal static binary likely will not work. I need to inspect the SPECIAL/syscall decoder and then build a freestanding MIPS binary with custom runtime/syscall stubs or a patched libc interface.",
  "plan": "Print the SPECIAL instruction dispatch around lines 1280-1360 to confirm syscall encoding, then inspect doomgeneric source dependencies and the img platform layer to plan the custom runtime.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/vm.js | sed -n '1280,1360p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -RhoE '\\b(memset|memcpy|memmove|memcmp|malloc|calloc|realloc|free|printf|fprintf|sprintf|snprintf|fopen|fread|fwrite|fclose|fseek|ftell|exit|abort|time|stat|strcmp|strcpy|strlen|strcat|strncmp|strncpy|atoi|abs|qsort)\\s*\\(' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/*.c | sed 's/(.*//' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -80\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
